<Article slug="best-ergonomic-chairs-under-600-singapore">
<p>You don't need to spend S$1,500 on a designer chair to get decent support for long WFH days. Below S$600, three chairs come up again and again for Singapore buyers. We compared what their makers publish: adjustments, weight limits, warranty and trial terms.</p>

<h2>Quick picks</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th>Chair</th><th>Best for</th><th>Price at time of writing (28 Oct 2026)</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>IKEA MARKUS</td><td>Tight budgets, and trying a chair in-store</td><td>around S$199</td></tr>
<tr><td>ErgoTune Joobie Lite</td><td>An entry-level mesh chair from a local brand</td><td>around S$349</td></tr>
<tr><td>ErgoTune Supreme</td><td>The most adjustment for long workdays</td><td>from around S$529 (sale)</td></tr>
</tbody></table>

<Product id="ikea-markus" rank={1} verdict="Best budget pick: a proven basic chair with a 10-year guarantee.">
<p>MARKUS has been one of IKEA's best-selling office chairs for years. IKEA Singapore listed it at around S$199 on 28 October 2026. According to IKEA, it has <strong>manually adjustable tilt tension</strong>, a built-in headrest and armrests, a <strong>10-year guarantee</strong>, and is <strong>tested for 110 kg</strong> to the ANSI/BIFMA X5.1 office chair standard.</p>
<p>The dark grey version's page showed an average rating of 4.6 out of 5 from 83 reviews when we checked.</p>
<p><strong>Watch out for:</strong> compared with dedicated ergonomic chairs, it has fewer adjustments. Check the product page for which parts adjust, especially the armrests and lumbar support, if you have specific back or shoulder needs. The 110 kg test weight is lower than the ErgoTune chairs below.</p>
</Product>

<Product id="ergotune-joobie-lite" rank={2} verdict="Best mid-range pick: a local brand's entry mesh chair.">
<p>ErgoTune is a Singapore brand, and the Joobie Lite is its lowest-priced chair. ErgoTune's site listed it at around S$349 on 28 October 2026. The range is sold with <strong>free shipping</strong>, a <strong>6-year warranty</strong> and a <strong>3-week free trial</strong>, according to ErgoTune.</p>
<p>A free trial matters a lot for chairs bought online, because fit is personal. It lets you return the chair if it doesn't suit your body.</p>
<p><strong>Watch out for:</strong> as the "Lite" model it has fewer adjustment points than the Supreme. Compare the adjustment table on ErgoTune's site to check it covers what you need.</p>
</Product>

<Product id="ergotune-supreme" rank={3} verdict="Best overall under S$600: lots of adjustment and a published 130 kg capacity.">
<p>The Supreme was ErgoTune's first chair, and the company calls it its most-reviewed. Its product page showed <strong>933 reviews, 77% of them 5-star</strong>, when we checked on 28 October 2026. It was on sale from around S$529 (regular price S$649).</p>
<p>ErgoTune lists <strong>13 adjustment points</strong>, including a headrest that adjusts in height, depth and angle; "ATLAS" lumbar support with tension settings; seat height and depth; and armrests that pivot. Other published specs:</p>
<ul><li>Breathable fabric mesh, useful in Singapore's heat</li><li>Aluminium base</li><li>User height range 140 to 200 cm, in Small, Medium and Large sizes</li><li>User weight range up to <strong>130 kg</strong></li><li>Chair weight 23.2 kg, warranty up to 6 years</li></ul>
<p><strong>Watch out for:</strong> pick the right size (Small for about 140 to 159 cm, Medium for 160 to 179 cm, Large for 180 cm and up), because it changes the seat height range.</p>
</Product>

<h2>What to look for in an ergonomic chair</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Adjustable lumbar support</strong> that sits in the small of your back.</li>
<li><strong>Seat depth adjustment</strong>, so you can leave about two to three fingers' gap between the seat edge and the back of your knees.</li>
<li><strong>Armrests</strong> that drop low enough to sit level with your desk, so your shoulders stay relaxed.</li>
<li><strong>Mesh vs foam.</strong> Mesh breathes better in Singapore's humidity, while foam can feel softer.</li>
<li><strong>A trial period or showroom.</strong> Comfort is personal, so try one in person or buy where you can return it.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Bottom line</h2>
<p>On a tight budget, the <strong>IKEA MARKUS</strong> at about S$199 is a safe, long-guaranteed starting point. For the most adjustment under S$600, the <strong>ErgoTune Supreme</strong> has the strongest published specs and the most reviews. The <strong>Joobie Lite</strong> sits in between and comes with ErgoTune's free trial.</p>
</Article>
